<caml:Content xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#"><p>In addition to the jurisdiction conferred by Section 116.220, the small claims court has jurisdiction in an action brought by a natural person, if the amount of the demand does not exceed twelve thousand five hundred dollars ($12,500), except as otherwise prohibited by subdivision (c) of Section 116.220 or subdivision (a) of Section 116.231.</p></caml:Content>